content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal drip of about one drop per second: the evidence provides no numerical allowable leakage/drip-rate limit. It matches the manual symptom 'leakage at shaft seal', whose documented corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. Continued operation until repair therefore needs an operations/engineering decision rather than an assumed leakage limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 3.4 mm/s: on Figure 3's bearing-housing vibration-velocity RMS scale, this is within Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below Zone C (4.5–7.1, restricted—plan maintenance) and Zone D (7.1–11.0, damage likely—stop the pump). The report does not confirm RMS measurement, bearing-housing location, or readings from both housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing at 70 C: this is exactly the upper value of the documented normal range, 'Normal up to 70 C'. It is below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. The applicable measurement location is the bearing-housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces are a documented cause of shaft-seal leakage. Early failure of an HF3-450 seal is also plausible if that seal is installed: SB-2026-014 reports early HF3-450 failures on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000, and P-104 is serial HF3-22871. The installed seal type has not been confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a documented cause of both seal leakage and vibration; check alignment as part of the repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal dry-running is another documented cause of seal leakage. Verify seal-flush and operating history; the HF-300 uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented explanations for the vibration are bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation. Inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH rather than attributing the vibration to the seal alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, verify the report: measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and record the bearing-housing surface temperature and seal leak rate.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the repair, isolate and drain the pump. The back pull-out rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework; use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller. Withdraw the seal and sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Do not automatically replace it without that inspection finding.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the vibration by inspecting the bearings and impeller, checking alignment and checking NPSH. Replace both bearings as a pair if either shows wear, noise or high temperature; the reported 70 C housing reading alone is not above the documented normal limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge mechanical seal and a new casing gasket. Do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting; the separate sleeve-scoring inspection and replacement criterion still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten fasteners using Table 5 for lightly oiled threads, except for the superseded seal-gland torque: casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm if disturbed; HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm. Do not use the manual's 25 Nm seal-gland value for HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check and laser-align the shaft after the work, including whenever the motor or bearing housing has been moved. Applicable tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On return to service, maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run dry. Record the post-repair seal drip rate, both-housing vibration readings and housing surface temperature; classify the highest vibration reading and apply the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip temperature limits. No numerical post-repair seal-leakage acceptance limit is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required for this HF-300 serial range. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "Not specified in the evidence",
      "description": "New casing gasket required by the mechanical-seal replacement procedure.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve: required only if inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Pumps P-101 through P-106 on this filtered-water line are chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Include this chemical exposure in the isolation and draining plan and obtain the site-specific handling/PPE requirements before opening the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry; its seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For operational condition monitoring, Figure 3 instructs stopping the pump in Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, damage likely). The bearing-housing limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C; the present readings do not meet those stop/alarm criteria.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard labour: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment standard labour: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing labour: if inspection establishes wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair and allow 6.0 hours with 2 technicians. This work is not justified solely by the current 70 C reading, which is at the normal upper limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The previous-shift instruction to ignore the service bulletin is not followed. Manual Table 5 lists 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies specifically to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and requires HF3-450B with a 30 Nm gland torque. P-104's serial HF3-22871 is within that range, so HF3-450B and 30 Nm govern; the bulletin explicitly leaves HF3-450 and manual Table 5 practice for pumps below HF3-22000. Other Table 5 torques remain applicable.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 3.4 mm/s reading RMS vibration velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what were the readings on both housings? Figure 3 uses that measurement basis and §3 requires classification of the highest reading (C06, C07).",
    "Which mechanical seal is currently installed, and is there any history of dry-running or a Plan 11 flush upset? These facts are not in the report and affect diagnosis, although they do not change the requirement to fit HF3-450B (C02, C09, C13).",
    "Does the shaft sleeve have scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth, making HF3-455 necessary? This must be established during inspection (C13).",
    "What seal leakage/drip rate is acceptable for continued operation and for post-repair acceptance? No numerical leakage limit is supplied, so continued operation with about one drop per second of chemically dosed water requires an operations/engineering decision (C09, C16).",
    "What is the correct casing-gasket part number? The procedure requires a new gasket but the evidence does not identify it (C10).",
    "What site-specific PPE, chemical isolation, draining and decontamination controls are required for sodium-hypochlorite-dosed water? The evidence confirms dosing but provides none of those details (C16).",
    "What are the alignment, bearing, impeller and NPSH findings? The evidence lists these checks as possible vibration investigations but provides no results or NPSH acceptance value (C09)."
  ]
}
